1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,000
There are women who never had the chance to sit in a classroom...

2
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:12,000
...yet, somehow, they understood the power of education better than anyone.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:18,500
They woke up before the sun, worked with tired hands...

4
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:25,000
...and carried dreams that were bigger than their own lives.

5
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:32,000
They watched the school gates from the outside...

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:38,500
They might not have known the answers to our homework...

7
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:45,500
...but they always knew one thing: we had to keep learning.

8
00:00:45,500 --> 00:00:52,000
With every quiet whisper to stay awake, they gave us wings.

9
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:58,000
Today, we are living the dreams they never had the opportunity to pursue.

10
00:00:58,000 --> 00:01:05,000
Every page we read, every door we open carries their sacrifice.

11
00:01:05,000 --> 00:01:11,000
They may never have called themselves teachers. But they were our first teachers.

12
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:17,000
And their wisdom will live through generations.

13
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:21,000
